  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "The manufacturing times of bicycle frames are normally distributed with a mean of $\\mu $ minutes and a standard deviation of $5$ minutes. Additionally, $25%$ of frames are completed in under $48$ minutes. Find the percentage of frames that take longer than $52$ minutes. **Round your answer to two decimal places.**\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.10\\,$ | $\\,0.20\\,$ | $\\,0.25\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-2.3263\\,$ | $\\,-1.8808\\,$ | $\\,-1.6449\\,$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ |\n\n*In addition, you're given the following table of values for $p=\u03a6(z)$*.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5517\\,$ | $\\,0.5557\\,$ | $\\,0.5596\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5910\\,$ | $\\,0.5948\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6293\\,$ | $\\,0.6331\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ |\n\nApproximately\n{{field-1}}$%$ of the frames take longer than $52$ minutes.",
